The Mercedes-Benz A180d is part of the current W177 generation A-Class (2018-present). It is typically powered by a 1.5L or 2.0L diesel engine producing around 116 hp and 260-280 Nm (192-207 lb-ft) of torque. Acceleration from 0-60 mph is around 9.0-10.6 seconds, and top speed is around 125-128 mph. It is a front-wheel-drive car with a 7-speed or 8-speed DCT automatic transmission.

Fuel economy is a strong point, with combined figures often in the 45-70 mpg range in real-world driving, and official figures higher. CO2 emissions are low, typically around 108-111 g/km. As a diesel, it has no electric range.

Dimensions are around 4419-4428 mm length, 1796 mm width, and 1440-1452 mm height, with a wheelbase of 2729 mm. Cargo space is around 341-370 liters (12.18-13.07 cu ft) with seats up. Rear legroom is around 33.9 inches. [Search needed, using A-Class general] Ground clearance is around 9.1-10.4 cm (3.58-4.1 inches). Turning circle is around 11-11.54 meters (36.09-37.86 ft). It has 5 seats.

New prices in the UK start around £31,300 - £35,000 (~$39k-$44k USD). Insurance groups are around 16-22. Maintenance costs are typical for a Mercedes. Reliability can be mixed, with some reports of issues like turbo lag/wear, DPF blockages, coolant leaks, steering rack problems, and MBUX glitches, though diesel engines are often robust.

The W177 A-Class received a 5-star Euro NCAP safety rating. ADAS features are available, though some are optional. Visibility can be average. [Search needed] Headlights are typically LED. Security features are standard Mercedes.

The MBUX infotainment system is a highlight, with standard dual 7-inch screens or optional dual 10.25-inch screens. The UX is generally well-regarded, with touchscreen, touchpad, and voice control ("Hey Mercedes"). Smartphone integration (Apple CarPlay/Android Auto) is standard/available. Audio systems are decent, with optional upgrades. Multiple USB-C ports are available.

Comfort and convenience features are good for the segment, with options like heated seats, dual-zone climate control, parking assist, and keyless entry.

Brand prestige is high (Mercedes-Benz). The A-Class is the entry-level model (high model prestige score). The A180d is an entry-level engine/trim (high trim prestige score). Interior luxury is good for the segment but not top-tier Mercedes. Interior tech focus is high due to the MBUX system.

The style is sleek and modern, with a moderately aggressive front end.

